    "Scouting Notes": "POST DRAFT NOTES\n This is a big man, standing at 6'8, and weighing 245\n Fastball is in the 92 94 range, touching 96, seems like a guy who could add some velo in pro ball\n Fastball has good carry, and he commands it super well to the top of the zone, though the shape plays down a bit due to the release height from such a tall guy\n Curveball is his best secondary, and a pitch he is extremely comfortable throwing in any count/situation. Solid shape, pretty decent spin\n Slider is an average tertiary pitch as well, and another that he has solid command of\n Changeup is the worst of his four pitches, but he shows flashes of being a fringe average pitch, which would go a long way\n Overall, there's untapped potential for a college guy. If he can add velo, and hold the command, there's a lot to like",
